WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.062 --> 00:00:03.430
Edward's rescuer was Miles.

2
00:00:03.431 --> 00:00:07.257
"This is a matter for the law to take care of."

3
00:00:07.258 --> 00:00:14.240
Miles held onto the blacksmith's arm until he released Edward. "Not you."

4
00:00:14.241 --> 00:00:18.994
The blacksmith rubbed his arm as Edward leaped to Miles' side.

5
00:00:18.995 --> 00:00:22.676
"I appreciate your rescuing me," Edward said.

6
00:00:22.677 --> 00:00:27.329
"But you took your time getting here, Sir Miles."

7
00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:31.566
"Sir Miles! I forgot that Edward made me a knight."

8
00:00:31.567 --> 00:00:34.113
Miles smiled to himself.

9
00:00:34.114 --> 00:00:38.226
"He's such a brave, spirited boy.

10
00:00:38.227 --> 00:00:43.966
I'm honored to be a knight—even if his kingdom is only an imaginary one."

11
00:00:43.967 --> 00:00:48.405
Miles' thoughts were interrupted by the arrival of the sheriff.

12
00:00:48.406 --> 00:00:51.512
"This must be the boy who stole the ham."

13
00:00:51.513 --> 00:00:54.616
The sheriff took out his handcuffs.

14
00:00:54.617 --> 00:00:57.701
"Don't handcuff him!" Miles said.

15
00:00:57.702 --> 00:01:01.046
"He'll go quietly to see the judge."

16
00:01:01.047 --> 00:01:05.074
But Edward was outraged and refused to move.

17
00:01:05.075 --> 00:01:08.814
"The king does not go to court!"

18
00:01:08.815 --> 00:01:15.252
"You can't expect your subjects to obey the law, if you won't," Miles said.

19
00:01:15.253 --> 00:01:20.045
"Hmm," Edward said. "You may be right.

20
00:01:20.046 --> 00:01:26.924
This will give me a chance to see how criminals are treated."

21
00:01:26.925 --> 00:01:31.636
*** Inside the courtroom the woman told her story to the

22
00:01:31.637 --> 00:01:34.217
judge. He quickly convicted Edward of

23
00:01:34.218 --> 00:01:38.953
theft. Miles gasped, but Edward stayed

24
00:01:38.954 --> 00:01:44.525
calm. "The poor boy doesn't realize he'll go to jail," Miles

25
00:01:44.526 --> 00:01:49.965
thought. "How much is this ham worth?" the judge asked the

26
00:01:49.966 --> 00:01:53.310
woman. "Five dollars," she

27
00:01:53.311 --> 00:01:58.663
said. The judge frowned. "Perhaps you'd like to think

28
00:01:58.664 --> 00:02:03.070
again. He's an ignorant lad, who was probably driven to steal by

29
00:02:03.071 --> 00:02:06.237
hunger." The woman folded her arms across her

30
00:02:06.238 --> 00:02:12.740
chest. "No, that's what the ham is worth, and he needs to be taught a

31
00:02:12.741 --> 00:02:15.480
lesson." The judge shifted in his

32
00:02:15.481 --> 00:02:22.878
seat. "You do know that the punishment for stealing anything over three dollars is life in

33
00:02:22.879 --> 00:02:29.547
prison?" Wide-eyed with fear, Edward looked at Miles, but Miles was too startled to comfort

34
00:02:29.548 --> 00:02:33.209
him. "Oh, what have I done?" the woman

35
00:02:33.210 --> 00:02:38.343
cried. "I don't want the boy to spend his life in

36
00:02:38.344 --> 00:02:43.301
prison!" "I haven't officially recorded the ham's value," the judge

37
00:02:43.302 --> 00:02:46.865
said. "There's still time for you to change

38
00:02:46.866 --> 00:02:53.491
it." "Oh, yes! Now that I think again, it's worth only a dollar at

39
00:02:53.492 --> 00:02:58.015
most." "That's better." The judge

40
00:02:58.016 --> 00:03:03.062
smiled. Miles hugged Edward, who let the big man embrace

41
00:03:03.063 --> 00:03:08.710
him. But when the judge sentenced him to five days in jail, Edward started to

42
00:03:08.711 --> 00:03:12.830
protest. "Hush!" Miles whispered as the judge stood up to leave.

43
00:03:12.831 --> 00:03:15.832
"Don't make the judge change his mind."

44
00:03:15.833 --> 00:03:20.642
"I didn't steal anything, so I shouldn't have to go to prison."

45
00:03:20.643 --> 00:03:24.062
Edward stamped his foot.

46
00:03:24.063 --> 00:03:29.943
Miles nodded but was busy watching the sheriff approach the woman.

47
00:03:29.944 --> 00:03:33.228
"I wonder what that fellow is up to."

48
00:03:33.229 --> 00:03:37.393
Miles walked over to where the sheriff and the woman were talking.

49
00:03:37.394 --> 00:03:44.614
"That's a fine ham," the sheriff said. "I'll buy it from you for a dollar."

50
00:03:44.615 --> 00:03:47.782
The woman was insulted by his offer.

51
00:03:47.783 --> 00:03:53.057
"I only said it was worth a dollar to spare the boy from life in prison.

52
00:03:53.058 --> 00:03:56.484
I paid five dollars for it."

53
00:03:56.485 --> 00:04:02.039
"So, you lied when you said it was worth a dollar!" the sheriff said triumphantly.

54
00:04:02.040 --> 00:04:06.709
"I guess the boy will spend the rest of his life in prison after all."

55
00:04:06.710 --> 00:04:11.812
"No, no!" The woman shook her head in confusion.

56
00:04:11.813 --> 00:04:17.541
Miles realized that the sheriff was trying to trick her, but he didn't say anything.

57
00:04:17.542 --> 00:04:23.647
After watching the woman sell the ham for a dollar, he returned to Edward's side.

58
00:04:23.648 --> 00:04:28.059
"I refuse to go to jail even for only five days."

59
00:04:28.060 --> 00:04:31.160
Edward stubbornly crossed his arms.

60
00:04:31.161 --> 00:04:35.134
"Don't worry, I have a plan," Miles said.

61
00:04:35.135 --> 00:04:40.804
"Just trust me, and we'll soon be on our way to my family's home."

62
00:04:40.805 --> 00:04:46.085
Having quickly hidden the ham, the sheriff was ready to escort Edward to jail.

63
00:04:46.086 --> 00:04:49.178
"Sheriff, we need to talk."

64
00:04:49.179 --> 00:04:52.892
Miles put his arm around the man's shoulders.

65
00:04:52.893 --> 00:04:57.920
"Perhaps you could look the other way while this boy escapes."

66
00:04:57.921 --> 00:05:01.581
"But I'd be committing a crime!" the sheriff said.

67
00:05:01.582 --> 00:05:05.620
"I should arrest you for even suggesting that!"

68
00:05:05.621 --> 00:05:10.311
"Or perhaps you'll be arrested." Miles paused.

69
00:05:10.312 --> 00:05:15.032
"I heard you trick the woman into selling you her ham.

70
00:05:15.033 --> 00:05:18.708
Do you want me to tell the judge about that?"

71
00:05:18.709 --> 00:05:26.096
"Oh, I was just joking with her!" The sheriff laughed nervously.

72
00:05:26.097 --> 00:05:29.568
"Really?" Miles said loudly.

73
00:05:29.569 --> 00:05:35.166
"You do know the penalty for breaking that law is death?"

74
00:05:35.167 --> 00:05:40.167
"What law?" The sheriff looked frightened.

75
00:05:40.168 --> 00:05:45.483
"The one against paying too little for big pieces of meat.

76
00:05:45.484 --> 00:05:50.524
You'd better return that ham to the woman and let Edward go."

77
00:05:50.525 --> 00:05:55.790
"Of course! Right away!" The sheriff hurried off.

78
00:05:55.791 --> 00:05:58.959
"I'll tell the judge that the boy simply disappeared."

79
00:05:58.960 --> 00:06:03.907
"Thank you!" Miles said.

80
00:06:03.908 --> 00:06:09.052
"How did you know about that law?" Edward asked as they left the courtroom.

81
00:06:09.053 --> 00:06:15.209
Miles smiled. "I made it up!"

